                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "685b6391-bfbc-31f2-9601-eb03d9c47658",
                        "entry_id": "21958dae-0548-369c-90c6-dbe9d2e390b0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To join mutually; to unite."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "72f688e5-7b97-47f3-96f0-04c78c6ff0b7",
                                "sense_id": "685b6391-bfbc-31f2-9601-eb03d9c47658",
                                "text": "[…] so, fellest foes,\nWhose passions and whose plots have broke their sleep,\nTo take the one the other, by some chance,\nSome trick not worth an egg, shall grow dear friends\nAnd interjoin their issues."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e859d6a8-0121-4195-931b-edb6cf9d13c8",
                                "sense_id": "685b6391-bfbc-31f2-9601-eb03d9c47658",
                                "text": "[…] it is most probable to be the Port of Trapezonment, plac’d in a Corner of the Euxine Sea; for from this Port, within a few Months, Anno 1272. they came to Ancona, which could not be perform’d from the Caspian Sea, by reason of the great space of Land and Regions interjoin’d."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0905192f-dcf4-47a9-9369-f5d505c93887",
                                "sense_id": "685b6391-bfbc-31f2-9601-eb03d9c47658",
                                "text": "The Kuzzauk salutation is made, by interjoining the four hands."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aae2e527-26a5-4a1e-8637-49f1d1a1df5d",
                                "sense_id": "685b6391-bfbc-31f2-9601-eb03d9c47658",
                                "text": "[…] seek the quoin\nWhere choir and transept interjoin,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89ebd4c8-e42b-4e9a-9fad-f101983d6537",
                                "sense_id": "685b6391-bfbc-31f2-9601-eb03d9c47658",
                                "text": "He feebly lifted an arm, but the darkness was even greater inside the shroud, and all he could see was a myriad of interjoining cracks."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6f1151d3-9412-3606-bdd0-b0d141768afa",
                        "entry_id": "21958dae-0548-369c-90c6-dbe9d2e390b0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To say by way of interruption, to interject."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e092573e-d8fc-472c-a761-431a5d6f0a97",
                                "sense_id": "6f1151d3-9412-3606-bdd0-b0d141768afa",
                                "text": "“No, no,” cried lady Anna, in trepidation, “leave him—let him go.”\nLennard unloosed his hold for a moment; and regarding her ladyship with a look of jealous anger, he stood irresolute.\n“Leave him,” interjoined Wentworth. “He has abused the privileges of a social meeting, by venting the preconcerted acumen of a malicious nature; he is beneath your contempt.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "053fc6a0-77df-4a49-90bc-e333fb620a2a",
                                "sense_id": "6f1151d3-9412-3606-bdd0-b0d141768afa",
                                "text": "“Oh! you can have no idea of its gaiety,” returned Frances; “and such a quantity of people.”\n“A number of persons, and a quantity of goods,” interjoined Miss Colville."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3fa552b3-bed5-40f1-ab7d-e7918fb35f12",
                                "sense_id": "6f1151d3-9412-3606-bdd0-b0d141768afa",
                                "text": "1899, Kate Chopin, The Awakening, Chicago and New York: Herbert S. Stone, Chapter 5, pp. 26-27,\n“Perhaps I feared to make Alphonse jealous,” she interjoined, with excessive naïveté. That made them all laugh."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a84e84da-0277-4f98-931a-8d8d78d0fc9d",
                                "sense_id": "6f1151d3-9412-3606-bdd0-b0d141768afa",
                                "text": "“[…] If the notice is not too short for you, Fossick, why not join us?”\n“A capital plan, Fossick,” interjoined the judge […]"
                            }
                        ]
